r_play":-0.03681,"pass_rate":0.4667,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4861,"def_epa_per_play":-0.5693},{"week":10,"opponent":"NYJ","home":false,"pf":31.0,"pa":12.0,"off_snaps":51,"epa_per_play":0.2965,"pass_rate":0.4314,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4,"def_epa_per_play":-0.09666}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"CHI","distance":0.6273,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":0.6345,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2022,"team":"CAR","distance":0.6835,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.7009,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2025,"team":"SEA","distance":0.7361,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Klint Kubiak"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.2004,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"IND","distance":0.2679,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2025,"team":"NE","distance":0.3342,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.3383,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DAL","distance":0.3906,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Bills are 8-1 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 287 to 199. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 4th in EPA per play while the defense sits 12th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive trait is the highest under center rate in the league.","offense":"The Bills have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in all five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the highest under center rate and the lowest shotgun rate in the league. Josh Allen has run the passing game, with Khalil Shakir leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Bills defense has been a little above average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 3rd, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 20th. Gregory Rousseau has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is T.J. Parker, who has 3.5 sacks while playing only 35% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 6th highest in the league.","special":"The Bills have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 64% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their secondary was among the youngest in the league.","players":"Josh Allen has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,223 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Khalil Shakir and Dalton Kincaid leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. James Cook has handled most of the work in the backfield with 85% of the carries. On defense, Gregory Rousseau leads the team with 8 sacks and Davison Igbinosun has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Joe Brady is calling the offense as head coach and Jim Leonhard is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Bears and the 2024 Lions, both under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Packers and the 2025 Colts under Lou Anarumo.","trends":"The offense went from 3rd in EPA per play in 2025 to 4th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 13th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 12th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was eight man box rate, which went from 5% to 10%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}